</node>
<node id="claim_s_promotes_reconstruction_and_oer">
  <data key="d16">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d17">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d27">surface-reconstruction mechanism</data>
  <data key="d28">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d29">mixed</data>
  <data key="d18">Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to theoretical calculations, operando Raman, and ex situ characterizations.</data>
</node>
